  "aiContextParagraph": "For the fifth weekend in a row, large-scale demonstrations have taken place across France, involving a coalition of students, labor unions, the Yellow Vest movement, and various activists. The movement, which has previously drawn hundreds of thousands of participants, is currently focused on economic pressures including the cost of living, as well as concerns regarding educational budget allocations. A primary point of contention is a proposed police law, which critics argue grants excessive authority to security forces. While government sources reported lower participation numbers compared to previous weeks, organizers maintained higher estimates of attendees. Reports indicate that although many of the gatherings remained peaceful, some urban areas experienced confrontations between protesters and security personnel, resulting in the use of tear gas by police. The demonstrations follow an ongoing period of public dissatisfaction linked to the broader national budget and legislative priorities.",
